'''Wilderness and Undead Pirates'''

* Hotfixes from last week:
** The Elder Chaos Druids’ teleblock is now correctly removed upon leaving the Wilderness.
** We've also stopped those pesky Druids from closing your bank if you'd recently been in combat.
** Drop rate of the Teleport Anchoring Scroll from the Zombie Pirate's Locker has been made 1 in 275.
** The Teleport Anchoring Scroll is no longer doubled when obtained from the Locker.
** Zombie Pirate Keys now drop at a rate of 1 in 24. On average, assuming you use up all of the keys you obtain, this makes the Teleport Anchoring Scroll around 4 times more common.
* Reduced the wander range of Elder Chaos Druids.
* Artio, Callisto, Calvar'ion, Spindel, Vet'ion and Venenatis won't attack for a short period after respawn, giving you the chance to manage your supplies and Inventory if needed.
* Increased the despawn timer of consumables dropped in the Wilderness to 15 seconds.
* Fixed an issue stopping you picking up loot on a particular tile at the Chaos Temple.

'''Wilderness Agility Course'''

* Hotfixes:
** The rope swing can now be used by more than one player at a time.
** The dispenser now provides Blighted Super Restores.
* Moved the location of Clue Steps inside the Wilderness Agility Course to a slightly quieter spot.
* Players can now take a pause between Wilderness Agility Course laps by logging out, although they will lose 25 laps for doing so. Leaving the arena or dying will still end the streak.
* The skeletons on the surface of the Wilderness Agility Course now deal less damage. Watch out though, underground Skeletons still hit for a max of 4.
* Damage now correctly applies through the ladder animation in the Wilderness Agility Course.
* The Wilderness Agility Course lap streak and loot now display while Game Chat is set to 'Filtered'.
* When paying the 150,000 GP fee to use the Agility Course, you'll now receive a looting bag if you don't currently own one.
* The Ring of Wealth(i) now interacts properly with Medium Clue Scrolls at the Wilderness Agility Course.
* The spikes underneath the Wilderness Agility arena no longer stop projectiles from travelling over them.

'''Varlamore '''

* Added Combat Achievements for the Colosseum and Perilous Moons.
* Removed a tree blocking the path in Fortis Park.
* Soar Leader Pitri now gives instructions about charging the Quetzal Whistle.
* The Fortis Crop circle will now spawn correctly, letting you teleport to Puro Puro.

'''Colosseum'''

* Colosseum acid pools no longer deal damage between waves.
* When using Dizana's Quiver alongside a Twisted Bow, the correct Ranged Strength stats will be used when firing Dragon Arrows.
* Updated the Manticore’s examine text.
* The Serpent Shaman's Water Surge now looks even more impressive!
* Updated the Quiver's appearance for both the standard variants and the Max Cape version.

'''Perilous Moons'''

* During the Eclipse Moon Orb special attack, you're now able to avoid taking damage when standing behind the orb.

'''Other Changes'''

* Removed the 2024 Easter Event.
* Wall Beasts in the Lumbridge Swamp Caves will now stay ''inside ''the walls.
* The new left-click options on the polar and jungle eagles now work for completing the relevant Achievement Diary tasks.
* Fixed an issue with the Collection Log search function on mobile, so you'll now be able to check your wins wherever you are.
* Justiciar is now categorised correctly as metal armour by Ava's devices.
* Resolved a crash issue observed inside the PoH dungeon under specific circumstances.

