==Third-party Client Guideline Updates==
In other news, we’re updating our guidelines for Third-Party Clients, including RuneLite and HDOS.

Firstly, we're removing the following from our 'disallowed features' list:

* Any plugin which unhides, hides or moves components of the Spellbook Interface.
** Resizing components of the Spellbook interface is still prohibited.
* Any plugin which adds additional menu entries which cause actions to be sent to the server.
** This one now includes exceptions for the Max Cape and Diary Cape.
* Any plugin which modifies menu options for Construction, such as prioritising build or remove options.

We’re allowing players to change elements of the Spellbook largely to give people greater flexibility over their gameplay experience. Most of our interfaces are over two decades old, and difficult to work with, but this legacy shouldn’t discourage us from giving players more freedom to make the UI comfortable. This change also gives ''us ''the flexibility to add new spells without worrying that we’ll mess up people’s muscle memory, as was the case with the new Teleport to Kourend requirement.

Next, we’re allowing players to add additional menu entries specifically to allow for Max Cape and Diary Cape usability improvements. As we add more teleport options, the menus become harder to navigate – so we’re allowing small tweaks that spare players from clicking through multiple dialogue boxes.

Saving the spiciest for last, we’re allowing players to modify menu options for the Construction skill. This is something we’d like to roll out to our own client at some point, and springs from a desire to make ‘traditional’ Construction training more approachable. Such changes won’t improve XP rates, but they ''will ''save your wrists!

These changes go into effect immediately, though you might have to wait a little while for our talented community developers to make the best use of these updated guidelines!

==GAME JAM V==
We’re gearing up for our fifth internal game jam! This is the time of year when our devs come together to work on passion projects. In the past, this work has led to content like Scurrius, Project Rebalance, and Perilous Moons – so we can’t wait to see what the team comes up with this time!

Game Jam V will run from April 22nd through to May 6th, which means April 24th will be a smaller update than usual, and May 1st will see no update at all – although '''there may still be downtime.'''

We’ll be sharing what the team gets up to using the '''#OSRSGameJam''' hashtag – so keep your eyes peeled!

==Coming Soon: Updated 'Report Abuse' Interface==
Next week will bring some usability improvements to the in-game ‘Report Abuse’ interface. The current menu is awkward in various ways – it can be interrupted during combat, cannot be opened while in another menu, and on Mobile the keyboard obscures the interface completely!

So, here's an updated version to address all three of these problems, which you can expect to see next week. Hooray!

[[File:Undead Pirates Tweaks, Varlamore CAs & More (3).png|516px|center]]

* This opens in the chatbox area rather than covering your game view, so it doesn't need to be dismissed by combat.
* That also means it can stay open while menus like the bank are in use.
* Plus, it won't be hidden under the keyboard on mobile devices.
* We've enabled a keyboard short-cut for each rule, too. For example, '7' would report this player for macroing, or '9' would report them for advertising websites. This may be handy if you're often sending reports for the same few rules.
* The menu's scrollbar remembers its position, too, where possible, so you hopefully won't have to scroll up and down too much when you use the menu.

If you need to type or edit the name of the player you're reporting, that can be done in the Chat Box too:

[[File:Undead Pirates Tweaks, Varlamore CAs & More (4).png|517px|center]]
As a little extra feature, we're also adding a right-click option to the congratulatory messages you receive when you PK someone, making it easier to report them if you think they were suspicious:

[[File:Undead Pirates Tweaks, Varlamore CAs & More (5).png|434px|center]]
Now, while the game team is trying to improve what we can about the game's menus to help you report rule-breakers, the back-end systems are not changing in this particular update. This means that other rules, like not being able to report someone if they haven’t spoken or traded recently, will remain unchanged.

Rest assured that our colleagues in the Player Support and Anti-Cheating teams are doing all they can to root out the rule-breakers from our community, and they do appreciate the in-game reports you sent them. We hope that next week’s update will make it easier for you all to help them out!

An extra feature you may notice is the 'Law-breaking content' button. We've added this new button to make it more straightforward to report illegal content to us. Very rarely, you may see chat related to illegal topics that are not fully covered by our game rules. For now, reporting illegal content is restricted to residents of [https://www.gov.uk/eu-eea#:~:text=EU%20countries&text=Austria%2C%20Belgium%2C%20Bulgaria%2C%20Croatia,%2C%20Slovenia%2C%20Spain%20and%20Sweden. EU Member State countries], although we may expand this rule in future.

To be clear, most of the rule-breaking behaviour players encounter is already covered by our game rules, and in those situations, the regular in-game 'Report' option is the best way to let us know about the issue.

